        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "02c8b1df-99e4-55f7-8872-c2361782733d",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Ziegfeld Follies\n- People: Lemuel Ayers, Roy Del Ruth, Robert Lewis, Vincente Minnelli, Merrill Pye, George Sidney, Charles Walters, Fred Astaire, Lucille Ball, Lucille Bremer, Fanny Brice, Judy Garland, Kathryn Grayson, Lena Horne, Gene Kelly, James Melton, Victor Moore, William Powell, Red Skelton, Esther Williams, Irving Brecher\n- Companies: Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer\n- Topics: American film actors, dancers, screenplays\n\nFacts:\n- Lucille Bremer was born on February 21, 1917, and she was an American film actress and dancer.\n- Irving Brecher wrote the screenplay for \"Shadow of the Thin Man\" in 1941.\n- Ziegfeld Follies is a 1946 American musical comedy film released by Metro-Goldwyn-Mayer.\n- Ziegfeld Follies was directed by Lemuel Ayers, Roy Del Ruth, Robert Lewis, Vincente Minnelli, Merrill Pye, George Sidney, and Charles Walters.\n- Ziegfeld Follies stars Fred Astaire, Lucille Ball, Lucille Bremer, Fanny Brice, Judy Garland, Kathryn Grayson, Lena Horne, Gene Kelly, James Melton, Victor Moore, William Powell, Red Skelton, and Esther Williams.\n- Fanny Brice was the only member of the Ziegfeld Follies ensemble who had been a star of the original Follies.\n- Irving Brecher wrote the screenplay for \"Ziegfeld Follies\" in 1946.\n- Irving Brecher wrote the screenplay for \"Bye Bye Birdie\" in 1963.\n- Lucille Bremer died on April 16, 1996.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
